A||||5||FieroMike||Signal Light Problem!!
Z||000000||FieroMike||04-09-99||09:41 AM||||I just got my car about three days ago and everything was fine.  Yesterday the signals stopped working, so I checked the fuse and it was blown!  No problem, I put a new one in.  Everytime I start driving forward it pops, and then I will put a new one in and it will work until I turn off the car and roll forward again!  I traced the circuit in my manual to the reverse light switch, which was not grounded, so I grounded it and replace every bulb on my car. (They were all dim anyway)  Now I have a reverse light and bright lights but the signal still blows a fuse!!  Any ideas? <br>p.s. Sometimes the radio face will go blank when I hit the brakes. (Loose wire? Couldn't see one!) Thanx for any help
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-09-99||09:56 AM||||Did you check <b>all</b> fuses? Sometimes when a fuse blows, the circuit can still get power from another circuit causing that circuit to overload.
Z||000002||FieroMike||04-09-99||10:19 AM||||I checked all the fuses, and the back of the fuse block to look for other problems.  For some reason it only does it when the car starts moving, it will work forever just sitting there.  I think there HAS to be a loose wire that moves when the car does. ???
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||04-09-99||10:32 AM||||So let me get this straight: you replace the fuse, but as soon as your car moves forward, the fuse blows, even when you aren't using the turn-signals? You also said: "it will work until I turn off the car and roll forward again". Does this mean the fuse blows with your ignition turned off? And the forward motion of your car alone is enough?
Z||000004||PaUL||04-09-99||04:07 PM||||hmmmm.....water in your taillights maybe?
Z||000005||FieroMike||04-12-99||10:25 AM||||Cliff, Paul,<br>The blue wire off the back of the fuse box is ground to a black wire in a wire harness by the reverse light switch by the stick.  This goes out through the firewall, the ground wire (or switch wire?) was melted by the exhaust and when I took off it swung up against the pipe and grounded out.  I put a new wire in there and tied it up against the firewall. All better!!!!! Thanks
